Your rules for this feature, as the builders will follow them (each one applies to every case like it, not just the example):
  1. Whenever an order is placed, it earns one loyalty point for every full Rs 100 of the item total after any discount code, rounded down (items of Rs 1,250 after the discount earn 12 points). Shipping and tax never count towards points. For example, with Rs 2,000 of goods, Rs 100 shipping, Rs 100 tax and a Rs 500 discount code, only the Rs 1,500 of goods after the discount earns points.
  2. Whenever an order is paid with store credit, it earns no loyalty points.
  3. Whenever the items on an order come to under Rs 500 after the discount code, the order earns no loyalty points.
  4. Whenever an order is a final-sale order, it earns double the loyalty points it would otherwise earn.
  5. Whenever a daily summary is made, an order belongs to the day it was placed on by the shop's own India-time clock, whatever day the server's time zone records. For example, an order placed at 11:50 pm India time on Monday belongs to Monday's summary. The report summarises whatever orders it is given.
  6. Whenever a customer asks to return an item because they changed their mind, count the days from delivery to the request (a negative count is treated as day 0). On days 0 to 14 (day 14 included) the refund is the full amount. On days 15 to 30 the refund is half the amount. After day 30 the request is not accepted and there is no refund. The amount is the item prices times quantities, minus any discount code, i.e. what the customer paid for the items. Tax is not part of the rules. No restocking fee or pickup deduction is ever taken. Example: Priya on day 3 and Arjun on day 10 get full refunds, and a customer on day 45 gets nothing.
  7. Whenever goods arrive damaged or defective, the customer gets a full refund if the request is made within 90 days of delivery, even if that is past the normal return period. After 90 days there is no refund. This also applies to final-sale orders. For example, a defective blender reported 20 days after delivery gets a full refund.
  8. Whenever a refund is worked out, shipping is never refunded, unless the goods arrived damaged or defective, in which case the shipping fee is refunded too.
  9. Whenever a refund amount is worked out, round it down to whole rupees. Whenever the refund is under Rs 50, it is not paid, except for damaged goods, which are paid even when under Rs 50.
  10. Whenever a refund is approved, pay it back to the original payment method: an order paid with store credit is refunded as store credit, and an order paid by card is refunded to that card.
  11. Whenever a refund is requested on an order that has already been refunded, refuse it.
  12. Whenever an order is a free Rs 0 gift order, its refund is Rs 0.
  13. Whenever the daily summary is made, its order count is every order in the "Orders" list, store-credit orders included.
  14. Whenever the daily summary is made, its revenue is the sum, over card orders only, of (item total after discount + shipping). Store-credit orders add nothing to revenue.
  15. Whenever the daily summary is made, its average order value is the revenue divided by the number of card orders, rounded down to a whole rupee. If there are no card orders, it shows 0, not "no sales". For example, orders of Rs 1,000, Rs 1,000 and Rs 1,001 show Rs 1,000 only if they are all card orders.
